## Can I withdraw?
You can stop at any time without giving a reason. You can ask for your data to be deleted up to {{ p.withdrawal }} after taking part by emailing the research team with your participant number. After this, your data are anonymised and cannot be removed.

## What happens to my data?
UCL is the data controller. Your data are stored securely on {{ p.storage }} under a participant number; your name and contact details are kept separately. {% if d.data_recipients %}Pseudonymised data will be accessed by our partner(s): {% for r in d.data_recipients %}{{ r.organisation }} ({{ r.country }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. {% endif %}Anonymised data are kept for {{ p.retention_years }} years{% if p.open_data %} and may be shared with other researchers via the UCL Research Data Repository{% endif %}. Results will be published at group level only.

The legal basis for processing your personal data is "public task". {% if d.special_category %}The legal basis for processing special category data (e.g. health{% if "ethnicity" in p.demographics %}, ethnicity{% endif %}) is "research purposes". {% endif %}See the UCL general privacy notice for participants in research: https://www.ucl.ac.uk/legal-services/privacy/ucl-general-research-participant-privacy-notice

